islamist militants have killed dozens of  civilians in northern mozambique  an armed group is holding the town of  palma under siege  it is a hub for international gas  projects worth some 60 billion dollars  the mozambique government says hundreds  of local people and foreign workers have  been rescued  and the french energy group total has  suspended work on a huge construction  project  mozambique's defense ministry says it is  working to restore normality  the defense and security forces  reinforced their operational strategy to  contain the terrorists criminal attacks  and restore normality in palmer  they've carried out operational actions  in the last three days focused primarily  on the rescue of hundreds of national  and foreign citizens protection of  citizens  and their property  dw correspondent adrian kries was in  mozambique before the  latest fighting began and is following  developments from cape town  he sent us this update about the  situation in palma  we have a very poor part of the country  actually the poorest part of the country  a lot of people are unhappy that the  government is not  investing and the government is not  listening to them then few of them  radicalize and the security forces  respond with massive force  also attacking their families and people  who have nothing to do  with those radical people and hence they  radicalize more people so the whole  thing spiraled out of control and  although the government has been busy  over the past months to say well  everything is under control it is not  they've basically just been quite  successful in keeping journalists out  and  international observers from the area  but the situation is bad when we finally  managed to get there last month  we had terrifying stories from displaced  people in the camps there  you heard stories of children who were  taken away  father showed me the picture of a 16  year old daughter and said look they  just took her away  one year ago i haven't heard anything of  her you hear stories of decapitating of  villagers in front of the entire village  and  this has been happening for many months  it is still not clear though  what the group really wants but it  appears that it's much more about  power and influence than it is about  religion
 

